          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b8a2ac181df509eac03291889f72fe8403e2440c39bff687032c19a8ca5a0565:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/mcp/src/list-tabs-tool.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:ba7babfd0da29913d4c33908ae0dad20c3468f69673e93c990683dad65007fa8"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dd7d2fcfd7384cb4a3228f539431dffd",
      "statement": "`tabId` threads end to end: MCP tool files extract it from input and pass it through `page-actions.ts`/`page-context.ts` (with a `config.defaultTabId` fallback that the MCP server does not populate), `websocket-client.ts` merges it into `target.tabId`, the relay forwards the envelope unchanged, and the shared `BrijioBackgroundController` extracts `target.tabId` once per message via `extractTabId` (parsing the string to a number) and threads it into page-context, page-content, action, batch, and navigation handlers and their adapter interfaces.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/background-controller.ts#L1789-L1800",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:94d04d781b628de01e5183a7a8cab5ddb2ad71209152f397949f5d9b43805550:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/background-controller.ts#L560-L655",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1e3529641ba4a2e366b3fe981dad42f113bcdd240e2f34615f1a6a08322b8f59:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/mcp/src/page-actions.ts#L100-L130",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4b86e2c18fc63ae93092ca4f6a7737dfd91761895c47454fb9e0bc7047635d91:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/mcp/src/websocket-client.ts#L806-L836",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1e6f87e087989712fb73ea4f411d89f3af7c23eba1ff477fa4cf92e71e19f46d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f6a1903498b9463191de2cd8e4c8f7d2",
      "statement": "The shared page-reader helpers (`readActiveTabPage`, `performActiveTabAction`, `performActiveTabBatch`) use a provided numeric `tabId` directly and skip the active-tab query; when absent they fall back to `tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true })` and validate the URL is a regular HTTP/HTTPS page (returning `no_active_tab` or `unsupported_page` errors). With an explicit `tabId` the `isRegularPageUrl` check is skipped, so a targeted tab that has navigated to a restricted scheme surfaces `content_script_unavailable` or `regular_page_permission_required` instead.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/page-reader.ts#L117-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cd59dccd17a86c61349ee4ec61894255acc2f4a5f2f35ed3957cfb06099d6021:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/page-reader.ts#L204-L246",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5afe7212e68d19797447d093e7d0d29b5587d79df8a9780881b0322e5292658f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/page-reader.ts#L481-L500",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01a20c8ac7c644ee6fd3c5b762244a28b2602dba21521e476c6e1074d01d838d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e3e1f6f813624592a9e2163d9e4114e2",
      "statement": "`navigateActiveTabToUrl` in both extensions accepts an optional `tabId`: when provided it updates that tab directly via `tabs.update(tabId, { url })`; when absent it queries the active tab and returns `no_active_tab` if none exists. Navigation is wrapped in a 10-second timeout surfacing `timeout`/`navigation_failed` errors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://clients/extensions/chrome/src/background.ts#L678-L760",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8c8af62bd3f404b67d505e13927c704062dff0abb4ae8dbbefc252d8d829ddcf:"
        },
